# Vercel must never build or deploy anything but web/.
#
# The Python agent under backend/ talks to a USB radio. It cannot run in the
# cloud, and deploying it would put operator credentials on a server for no
# benefit. Vercel's framework detection finds backend/agent/pyproject.toml,
# sees FastAPI, and tries to deploy it — which is what broke the first build.
#
# The authoritative fix is the project's Root Directory setting (= "web").
# This file is a second line of defence.

backend/
docs/
*.md
!web/**

# Team secrets — never uploaded by a local `vercel` deploy either.
.env.team
.env*
!web/.env.example
